  "body": "## What changed\n\nPart alignment from two perpendicular edge picks (#769): the picks\ndefine the full 3D frame.\n\n- `pick::align_from_axes` (`crates/app/src/pick/axis.rs`): with both\n  +Y and +X picked, their directions - read through the setup's held\n  alignment, so it composes after a face lay - define the frame: the\n  primary axis lands exactly, the secondary is orthogonalized against\n  it (landing within the skew it came with), and +Z lands on the\n  picks' cross, the right-hand rule. The part turns about the centre\n  of its bounds; the origin is NOT set (the work offset stays where\n  it is placed). A left-handed pair is honoured literally (the part\n  lands as picked) instead of refused; only (nearly) parallel picks\n  refuse, by name. The landing is proved before the command stores\n  anything.\n- `AlignPartToSetup::align_from_axes` / `check_align`\n  (`commands/setup_align.rs`): the command constructors, same\n  refusals by name.\n- The UI axis panel (`egui_app/setup_axis_pick.rs`, the `CommandKind`\n  renamed `TurnPartInPlane` -> `AlignPartFromAxes`): same rows, same\n  picks, same flip toggles - the meaning grew. One picked axis keeps\n  the in-plane turn (#557 unchanged, `turn_in_plane` kept for its\n  callers); the words under Apply say which case applies.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/align_axes.rs` (9 tests): the user's exact\n  case (a down-Z edge picked +Y, a -X edge picked +X - full 3D\n  landing, the picks' cross up, centre unmoved); a vertical edge as +Y\n  lays the part on its side; in-plane picks subsume `turn_in_plane`\n  exactly (positions and rotation, pinned); one axis alone keeps the\n  in-plane turn; a skewed secondary lands within its own skew;\n  parallel picks refused by name; a left-handed pair honoured\n  literally (pinned as deliberate); picks compose after a held\n  alignment; a face pick still refuses by name.\n- New UI pin `two_picks_with_an_upright_edge_align_the_part_in_full_3d`\n  (setup_axis_tests): the round that #557 refused - upright edge +\n  top edge - leaves Apply on, applies, lands the picks on their axes\n  with +Z on their cross, never touches the work offset, and one undo\n  restores. Existing surface pins updated for the renamed command and\n  the new status words.\n- Battery green: align_axes 9, axis_align 10, plane_align 9,\n  points_align 8, turn_pivot 5, ui setup_axis 9; clippy clean on\n  camcraft-app and camcraft-ui.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The origin is untouched by design (the work-offset flows own it).\n- `turn_in_plane` and `in_plane_turn_deg` are unchanged; their callers\n  (single-pick panel round, MCP align tools) keep their behavior -\n  the MCP surface exposing `turn_in_plane` still turns in-plane only.\n\nChangelog: feat(align): part alignment from two perpendicular edge picks - the picks define the full 3D frame, +Z by the right-hand rule (#769, PR #770)\n\nFixes #769\n\n",
